menu "Opus"

config ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS
    bool "use TuyaOpen Opus instead of the platform libopus.a"
    default n
    help
        Disabled by default to use the platform SDK's prebuilt libopus.a.

        When enabled, CMake checks the Opus sources under
        src/tuya_ai_service/thirdparty/opus/upstream/ and downloads them if missing.
        Downloading requires Git and network access on the build host.
        Builds the portable fixed-point implementation with float APIs
        disabled. Opus objects are included in the SDK tuyaos archive.

config ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS_ARM_DSP
    bool "Use ARM DSP inline assembly for TuyaOpen Opus on T5AI"
    depends on ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS && PLATFORM_CHOICE = "T5AI"
    default n
    help
        Use upstream ARM fixed-point multiply and saturating arithmetic.
        CMake verifies DSP support with the selected cross compiler.
        No NEON or runtime CPU detection is required.

config ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS_CORTEX_M3_MUL
    bool "Use bit-exact Cortex-M3 SILK multiplication on L511G_Y7PM"
    depends on ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS && PLATFORM_CHOICE = "L511G_Y7PM"
    default n
    help
        Experimental SMULL implementations of SILK's four halfword
        multiply/accumulate macros. Preserve per-product rounding and
        the existing full-word multiplication definitions.
        CMake checks the selected compiler for ARMv7-M support.
        Disable this option to restore the portable fixed-point macros.

config ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS_NSQ_CACHE
    bool "Cache scalar state inside the normal NSQ sample loop"
    depends on ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS && (ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS_ARM_DSP || PLATFORM_CHOICE = "L511G_Y7PM")
    default n
    help
        Experimental T5AI/L511G_Y7PM normal-NSQ optimization. Preserve per-product
        rounding and final state updates; reduce scalar state memory traffic.
        T5AI caches five scalars; L511G_Y7PM caches only the shaping buffer index
        to limit Cortex-M3 register pressure.

config ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS_NSQ_RAM
    bool "Run normal NSQ from L511G_Y7PM internal MSMB RAM"
    depends on ENABLE_TUYAOPEN_OPUS && PLATFORM_CHOICE = "L511G_Y7PM"
    default n
    help
        Place silk_NSQ_c in the platform's existing MSMB RAM code section.
        The platform loader copies/decompresses it at boot and restores it
        on wake. Uses several KiB of internal RAM; the platform linker
        checks its shared RAM boundary. No codec arithmetic is changed.
        Independent of NSQ_CACHE so each optimization can be measured.

endmenu
